{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 ReaImGui front-end for folder-based POLY smart batch renders with per-item cover-art injection. Select items on the parent/folder track, then run the batch render. The script forces "selected media items via master", can disable the selected-item render tail to avoid the common +1 second output issue, and restores track/project state after rendering.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 For each selected parent item, the script reads the item's source image file and writes it to:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab ID3:APIC_FILE\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab FLACPIC:APIC_FILE before rendering that item.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Optional modules:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Inject UCS/ASWG metadata keys into Project Render Metadata\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Update next META marker RecType/Microphone/ixmlTrackLayout/ChannelLayout from active folder child tracks\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Post-write ixmlTrackLayout/ChannelLayout directly into rendered WAV/BWF files using bwfmetaedit\sa180\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Imports annotation TXT files as regions for each selected item. Each selected item looks for a matching TXT file (by item name) in the same directory and inserts regions offset to the item start.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Imports annotation TXT files and creates REAPER regions starting at the current edit cursor position. Commonly used for Chirpity, Audacity, BirdNET, or similar annotation exports.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Copies unique marker and region names that fall inside the current time selection to the clipboard, sorted by how often they appear (most frequent first). Output is comma-separated.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Select a folder parent track and place the edit cursor over audio/MIDI signal on its child tracks. The script finds the continuous child-track signal region under the cursor, then either stretches an overlapping image item on the folder track to that range or creates an empty named item there.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 ReaImGui front-end for Perch v2 and BirdNET detection. Keeps the existing non-UI Perch script untouched.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 Rename Takes from Clipboard + META Markers\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 This script reads a UCS-style {\f1 Filename="..."} string from the clipboard and renames selected REAPER takes accordingly.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Behaviour\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Keeps the plain filename if no duplicates exist\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Automatically numbers existing and selected takes (e.g. Base 01_suffix, Base 02_suffix)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Ignores currently selected takes when scanning existing ones\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Appends META project markers after item end\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Requirements\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab SWS Extension (CF_GetClipboard)\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Notes\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Designed for Soundminer / UCS workflows\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Safe to run multiple times\sa180\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Pre-populates Project Render Metadata with all UCS / Extended / ASWG keys (same mapping as acendan_UCS Renaming Tool) without renaming anything. Run before opening the Render dialog so fields aren\u8217't empty.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 By default writes $marker(Field)[;] substitutions (dynamic). Optional: set direct_values = true to write current extstate literal values instead.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Select item(s), choose a CSV file, META markers are generated from CSV rows whose CreationDate falls within the item's BWF origination time range.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 SRU ReaScripts\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Professional REAPER scripts for sound editing, sound-library metadata, annotation import, batch rendering, and wildlife-audio detection workflows.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Install With ReaPack\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 1.\tx360\tab Install {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://reapack.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
ReaPack
}}}
 for REAPER.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 2.\tx360\tab In REAPER, open {\b Extensions > ReaPack > Import repositories...}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 3.\tx360\tab Add this repository URL:\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \f1 https://raw.githubusercontent.com/SGMscripts/SRU/refs/heads/master/index.xml\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 4.\tx360\tab Open {\b Extensions > ReaPack > Browse packages}.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 5.\tx360\tab Search for {\f1 SGM} or {\f1 Sruthin}, install the scripts you need, then run them from REAPER's Action List.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Script Catalog\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 | Area | Script | Purpose | Requirements | | --- | --- | --- | --- | | Batch Render | {\f1 Batch Render/POLY Smart Batch Render IMGUI sruthin - Auto Cover Art.lua} | Folder-based POLY/stereo batch renders with cover art, UCS metadata, channel-layout patching, and child-media sample-rate matching. | ReaImGui, optional {\f1 bwfmetaedit} | | SFX Detection | {\f1 SGM-Perch-BirdNET/SGM Perch and Birdnet Detect .lua} | ReaImGui front-end for Perch v2 and BirdNET detection workflows. | ReaImGui, Python helper files | | Chirpity | {\f1 Chirpity/Chirpity analysis results to reaper regions SGM .lua} | Imports per-item annotation TXT files as REAPER regions. | REAPER | | Chirpity | {\f1 Chirpity/Chirpity Audacity  to reaper  with insertion offset SGM for Single item .lua} | Imports annotation TXT files at the edit cursor as regions. | REAPER | | Chirpity | {\f1 Chirpity/Copy Unique Marker Names in Time Selection to Clipboard SGM .lua} | Copies unique marker and region names from the time selection, sorted by frequency. | SWS Extension | | Item Editing | {\f1 Item/Align Highest Transient (Smart Priority- Hovered Item > Selection SGM v2.lua} | Aligns hovered or selected item transients to the edit cursor with overlap handling. | REAPER | | Item Editing | {\f1 Item/Create Folder Signal Region Item or Stretch Image SGM.lua} | Creates a folder-track region item from child-track signal under the cursor, or stretches an overlapping image item to that range. | REAPER | | UCS | {\f1 Ucsify/Add meta Marker and rename smart SGM.lua} | Renames takes from UCS clipboard data and adds META markers. | SWS Extension | | UCS | {\f1 Ucsify/Meta markers for selected items from ucsify csv SGM.lua} | Creates META markers from UCS CSV rows matching selected item BWF ranges. | SWS Extension | | UCS | {\f1 Ucsify/inject metaddata fileds SGM.lua} | Pre-populates project render metadata fields for UCS/ASWG workflows. | REAPER 6.33+ recommended |\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Repository Layout\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \f1 .\line
|-- Chirpity/             Annotation import and marker utility scripts\line
|-- Batch Render/         POLY batch render and cover-art workflows\line
|-- Item/                 Item editing utilities\line
|-- SGM-Perch-BirdNET/    Detection UI script and Python helper files\line
|-- Ucsify/               UCS metadata and META marker tools\line
|-- index.xml             ReaPack package index\line
`-- .github/workflows/    ReaPack validation and index deployment\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Development Notes\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Keep every installable script as a standalone {\f1 .lua} file with ReaPack metadata at the top.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Bump the {\f1 @version} field when changing script behavior.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Run {\f1 luac -p path/to/script.lua} before release when possible.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab GitHub Actions run {\f1 reapack-index --check} on pushes and pull requests.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab The {\f1 deploy} workflow updates {\f1 index.xml} after changes land on {\f1 master}.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Support\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Open an issue with the script name, REAPER version, operating system, installed extensions, and a short description of what happened. Screenshots or a small test project are helpful when the issue depends on project routing or metadata.\par}
}
